[{"category":"section","location":"reference/#Reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"module","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.MPSKitTaSK","page":"Reference","text":"Tangent-space Krylov (TaSK) spectral functions of finite matrix product states, built on MPSKit.jl (arXiv:2510.07279).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.MPSKitTaSK"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.LocalMPO","page":"Reference","text":"LocalMPO(Ws::Vector{<:MPOTensor})\n\nAn operator acting on length(Ws) consecutive sites, given as a local MPO [W_1, …, W_N]. The left virtual leg of W_1 must be trivial; the right virtual leg of W_N is the auxiliary leg of the operator, which carries the excitation sector of charged operators.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.LocalMPO"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.TaSK","page":"Reference","text":"TaSK(; krylovdim = 30, tol = MPSKit.Defaults.tol, verbosity = MPSKit.Defaults.verbosity, orth = KrylovKit.ModifiedGramSchmidt2(), kwargs...)\n\nTangent-space Krylov (TaSK) algorithm: a Lanczos recursion of the excitation Hamiltonian within the quasiparticle tangent space of a ground state (arXiv:2510.07279).\n\nverbosity follows the MPSKit levels (0: none, 1: warnings, 2: start/finish, 3: every Lanczos step), reporting the lowest Ritz value (obj, the lowest excitation energy resolved so far) and its residual norm (err).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.TaSK"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.TaSKResult","page":"Reference","text":"TaSKResult\n\nResult of a TaSK Lanczos run: poles energies with spectral weights (summing to b0^2), the Krylov tridiagonal matrix T_kr, the norm b0 of the projected initial state, the ground-state expectation value expval, the initial vector phi0 and the Krylov basis.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.TaSKResult"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK._excitation_sector-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:TensorKit.AbstractTensorMap{T, S, 2, 2} where {S, T}}}","page":"Reference","text":"Excitation sector carried by the auxiliary (rightmost) leg of a local MPO.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK._excitation_sector"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK._local_op_projection","page":"Reference","text":"_local_op_projection(Ws, gs, s::Int, left_gs = gs) -> (Φs, loc_ev)\n\nApply the local MPO Ws on sites s, …, s + N - 1 of gs (in mixed gauge around s) and return the effective one-site tensors Φs[i][l p; u r] at site s + i - 1, obtained by contracting all other sites with left_gs.AL (left) and left_gs.AR (right). The leg u is the auxiliary leg of W_N, which becomes the utility leg of the quasiparticle. Also returns ⟨gs|O|gs⟩ (zero for charged operators).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK._local_op_projection"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK._nsites-Tuple{TensorKit.AbstractTensorMap}","page":"Reference","text":"Number of sites an operator acts on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK._nsites"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK._set_qp_from_3leg!-Tuple{MPSKit.LeftGaugedQP, Int64, TensorKit.AbstractTensorMap{T, S, 2, 1} where {S, T}}","page":"Reference","text":"_set_qp_from_3leg!(qp::MPSKit.LeftGaugedQP, i::Int, ϕ::MPSKit.MPSTensor)\n\nProject a 3-leg tensor ϕ (Vleft ⊗ Vphys ← V_right) onto qp.VLs[i] and store in qp.Xs[i].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK._set_qp_from_3leg!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK._set_qp_from_4leg!-Tuple{MPSKit.LeftGaugedQP, Int64, TensorKit.AbstractTensorMap}","page":"Reference","text":"_set_qp_from_4leg!(qp::MPSKit.LeftGaugedQP, i::Int, ϕ)\n\nProject a 4-leg tensor ϕ (Vleft ⊗ Vphys ← Vutil ⊗ Vright) onto qp.VLs[i] and store in qp.Xs[i].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK._set_qp_from_4leg!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.broaden-Tuple{TaSKResult, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Reference","text":"broaden(res::TaSKResult, ω_grid; broadening = :gaussian, σ = 0.05, n_cfe = 2, η_reg = 1e-12) -> Vector\n\nBroadened spectral function of the TaSK poles on ω_grid, with broadening ∈ (:gaussian, :lorentzian, :cfe).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.broaden"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.cfe_broadening-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"cfe_broadening(energies::AbstractVector{<:Real}, weights::AbstractVector{<:Real}, ω_grid::AbstractVector{<:Real}, [σ::Real]; n_cfe::Int = 2, σ::Real = 0.05, η_reg::Real = 1e-12) -> Vector\n\nMoment-Preserving Continued Fraction Expansion (CFE) residual broadening from SM Sec. S-2 (Eqs. S22–S36) of arXiv:2510.07279v1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.cfe_broadening"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.correlator_spectrum-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Number}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Reference","text":"correlator_spectrum(times, C, ω_grid; σ = 0.05) -> Vector\n\nSpectral function from a real-time correlator C(t) = ∑ₙ wₙ exp(-i Eₙ t) sampled at times (starting at 0): S(ω) = (1/π) Re ∫₀ᵀ C(t) exp(i ω t) exp(-σ² t² / 2) dt (trapezoidal rule). For σ T ≫ 1 this equals the Gaussian broadening of the poles with width σ, cf. gaussian_broadening.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.correlator_spectrum"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.dawson-Tuple{Real}","page":"Reference","text":"dawson(x::Real)\n\nDawson's integral D₊(x) = exp(-x²) ∫₀ˣ exp(t²) dt, accurate to machine precision: the Maclaurin series ∑ₙ x²ⁿ⁺¹ / (n! (2n + 1)) (all terms positive, so free of cancellation) for |x| ≤ 7 and the asymptotic expansion (1 / 2x) ∑ₖ (2k - 1)!! / (2x²)ᵏ beyond.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.dawson"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.default_omega_grid-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:TaSKResult}}","page":"Reference","text":"Default frequency grid covering all poles of results with a margin of a few σ.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.default_omega_grid"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.dynamical_correlator","page":"Reference","text":"dynamical_correlator(H, O, gs, alg::TaSK = TaSK(); momentum, ω_grid, t_grid, broadening = :cfe, kwargs...)\n\nRun TaSK and return the poles together with the broadened spectral function S_ω on ω_grid and/or the real-time correlator C_t on t_grid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.dynamical_correlator"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.dynamical_structure_factor-Tuple{Any, MPSKit.AbstractMPS, AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Reference","text":"dynamical_structure_factor(O, gs, k_grid, omega_grid; H, alg = TaSK(), broadening = :cfe, kwargs...)\n\nMomentum-resolved dynamical structure factor S(k, ω) of O from one TaSK run per momentum. Returns a named tuple with k_grid, k_over_pi, omega_grid, S_kw (ω × k), peak_omegas, weights_sum and the individual results.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.dynamical_structure_factor"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.evaluate_correlator-Tuple{TaSKResult, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"evaluate_correlator(res::TaSKResult, t; include_disconnected = false)\n\nReal-time correlator C(t) = ∑ₙ wₙ exp(-i Eₙ t) (plus |⟨O⟩|² if include_disconnected).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.evaluate_correlator"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.gaussian_broadening-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"gaussian_broadening(energies::AbstractVector{<:Real}, weights::AbstractVector{<:Real}, ω_grid::AbstractVector{<:Real}, [σ::Real]; σ::Real = 0.05) -> Vector\n\nCompute Gaussian broadened spectral function: S(ω) = ∑ₙ Sₙ * (1 / (sqrt(2π) * σ)) * exp(- (ω - ωₙ)^2 / (2 * σ^2))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.gaussian_broadening"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.local_mpo-Union{Tuple{TensorKit.AbstractTensorMap{<:Any, S, N, N}}, Tuple{N}, Tuple{S}} where {S, N}","page":"Reference","text":"local_mpo(O) -> Vector{<:MPOTensor}\n\nDecompose an N-site operator O::AbstractTensorMap{T, S, N, N} into a local MPO [W_1, …, W_N] with trivial outer virtual legs, using MPSKit.decompose_localmpo(MPSKit.add_util_leg(O)). A LocalMPO is returned as is.\n\nThe left virtual leg of W_1 must be trivial. The right virtual leg of W_N is the auxiliary leg of the operator: trivial for symmetric operators, and carrying the excitation sector for charged ones (e.g. the spin-1 leg of spin_vector_operator).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.local_mpo"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.lorentzian_broadening-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"lorentzian_broadening(energies::AbstractVector{<:Real}, weights::AbstractVector{<:Real}, ω_grid::AbstractVector{<:Real}, [σ::Real]; σ::Real = 0.05) -> Vector\n\nCompute Lorentzian broadened spectral function with half width σ: S(ω) = ∑ₙ Sₙ * (σ / π) / ((ω - ωₙ)^2 + σ^2)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.lorentzian_broadening"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.plot_spectral_function","page":"Reference","text":"plot_spectral_function(res_dsf; title = \"Dynamical Structure Factor\", clims = nothing)\nplot_spectral_function(res::TaSKResult; ω_grid = nothing, broadening = :gaussian, σ = 0.05, n_cfe = 2)\nplot_spectral_function(results::AbstractVector{<:TaSKResult}, ks = 1:length(results); ω_grid = nothing, broadening = :gaussian, σ = 0.05, n_cfe = 2, logscale = false)\nplot_spectral_function(S::AbstractMatrix, ks, ω_grid; logscale = false)\n\nHeatmap of the dynamical structure factor returned by dynamical_structure_factor, overlaid with the peak positions; or the spectral function of a single TaSK result, or a heatmap of several (e.g. one per momentum ks, in units of π, shown on xlims = (0, 2)). With broadening = nothing the bare poles are shown instead, coloured by their weight; logscale = true colours by its logarithm (floored 10 decades below the maximum). A precomputed S[ω, k] (e.g. from tdvp_structure_factor) is plotted as a heatmap directly. Requires Plots.jl to be loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.plot_spectral_function"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent!","page":"Reference","text":"project_tangent!(\n    qp::MPSKit.FiniteQP, ops::AbstractVector, gs::MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS = qp.right_gs;\n    amplitudes = nothing, kwargs...\n) -> (qp, expval)\n\nIn-place projection of ∑ℓ amplitudes[ℓ] * ops[ℓ] |gs⟩ onto the 1-site tangent space qp::FiniteQP, where ops[ℓ] acts on the sites ℓ, …, ℓ + N - 1. Arbitrary N-site operators are supported by decomposing them into local MPOs (see local_mpo).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent-Tuple{AbstractVector, MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"project_tangent(ops::AbstractVector, gs::MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS, momentum::Real; amplitudes=nothing, left_gs=gs, sector=nothing, kwargs...)\n\nProject ∑ⱼ amplitudes[j] * exp(i k j) * ops[j] |gs⟩ at momentum k = momentum onto the finite quasiparticle tangent space of gs. k must be a multiple of 2π / length(gs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent-Tuple{AbstractVector, MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS}","page":"Reference","text":"project_tangent(ops::AbstractVector, gs::MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS; amplitudes=nothing, left_gs=gs, sector=nothing, kwargs...)\n\nProject a vector of local operators ops onto the finite quasiparticle tangent space of gs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent-Tuple{Any, Int64, MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS}","page":"Reference","text":"project_tangent(op, site::Int, gs::MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS; amplitude=1.0, left_gs=gs, sector=nothing, kwargs...)\n\nProject a single local operator op situated at site onto the tangent space of gs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent-Tuple{Any, MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"project_tangent(op, gs::MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS, momentum::Real; site=nothing, amplitude=1.0, amplitudes=nothing, left_gs=gs, sector=nothing, kwargs...)\n\nProject an operator op at momentum momentum onto gs::AbstractFiniteMPS: without site, op is placed on all possible positions with amplitude amplitude / √N_ops.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent-Tuple{Any, MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS}","page":"Reference","text":"project_tangent(op, gs::MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS; site = nothing, momentum = nothing, kwargs...) -> (qp, b0, expval)\n\nProject op|gs⟩ onto the one-site quasiparticle tangent space of the finite MPS gs and return the normalized tangent vector qp, its norm b0 and the ground-state expectation value expval = ⟨gs|op|gs⟩ (subtracted from the projection; zero for charged operators).\n\nop may be an N-site AbstractTensorMap, a LocalMPO, a vector of such operators (one per site) or a FiniteMPO/FiniteMPOHamiltonian. Without momentum, a single operator is placed at site (default: the centre of the chain); with momentum = 2πn/L, it is summed over all sites with the plane-wave amplitudes exp(i k j) / √N. pos and k are aliases of site and momentum.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent-Tuple{Union{MPSKit.FiniteMPO, MPSKit.FiniteMPOHamiltonian}, MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS}","page":"Reference","text":"project_tangent(O::Union{MPSKit.FiniteMPO, MPSKit.FiniteMPOHamiltonian}, gs::MPSKit.AbstractFiniteMPS; left_gs=gs, sector=one(sectortype(gs)), envs=nothing, kwargs...)\n\nProject an MPO or MPOHamiltonian onto the finite quasiparticle tangent space.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.project_tangent"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.spectral_map-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:TaSKResult}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Reference","text":"spectral_map(results::AbstractVector{<:TaSKResult}, ω_grid; kwargs...) -> Matrix\n\nBroadened spectral functions of several TaSK results (e.g. one per momentum) as a length(ω_grid) × length(results) matrix. Keyword arguments are passed to broaden.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.spectral_map"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.spectral_moments","page":"Reference","text":"spectral_moments(ω_grid::AbstractVector{<:Real}, S_ω::AbstractVector{<:Real}, max_order::Int = 4; max_moment::Int = max_order) -> Vector\n\nCompute spectral moments μk = ∫ ω^k S(ω) dω for k = 0, ..., maxmoment.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.spectral_moments"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.spin_exchange_operator","page":"Reference","text":"spin_exchange_operator([elt = ComplexF64], [SU2Irrep]; spin = 1 // 2) -> TensorMap\n\nThe SU(2)-invariant two-site Heisenberg exchange 𝐒ᵢ ⋅ 𝐒ⱼ = (S_tot(S_tot + 1) - 2s(s + 1)) / 2, e.g. as the dimer probe of task_spectrum. For abelian symmetries use MPSKitModels.S_exchange.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.spin_exchange_operator"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.spin_vector_operator","page":"Reference","text":"spin_vector_operator([elt = ComplexF64], [SU2Irrep]; spin = 1 // 2) -> LocalMPO\n\nThe spin vector operator 𝐒 as a one-site local MPO whose right virtual leg carries spin 1, obtained from the first factor of the local MPO of 𝐒ᵢ ⋅ 𝐒ⱼ and normalized to 𝐒 ⋅ 𝐒 = s(s+1). For an SU(2)-symmetric ground state, its spectral function is ∑ₐ Sᵃᵃ(k, ω) = 3 Sᶻᶻ(k, ω).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.spin_vector_operator"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.tangent_variance_2site","page":"Reference","text":"tangent_variance_2site(H, phi::MPSKit.QP, lenvs = ..., renvs = ...; envs = nothing, alg_environments = MPSKit.Defaults.alg_environments())\n\nCompute the 2-site tangent-space leakage variance σ^{2⊥} = || P^{2⊥}{ψg} H |Φ⟩ ||^2 (Eq. S18 of arXiv:2510.07279v1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.tangent_variance_2site"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.task_lanczos","page":"Reference","text":"task_lanczos(H, phi0::MPSKit.QP, alg::TaSK = TaSK(), lenvs = nothing, renvs = nothing; kwargs...) -> TaSKResult\n\nRun the TaSK Lanczos recursion of the effective excitation Hamiltonian of H starting from the tangent vector phi0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.task_lanczos"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.task_spectrum","page":"Reference","text":"task_spectrum(H, O, gs::MPSKit.AbstractMPS, alg::TaSK = TaSK(); site, momentum, kwargs...) -> TaSKResult\n\nProject O|gs⟩ onto the quasiparticle tangent space of the finite MPS gs (at site, or summed over the chain at momentum ∈ 2π/L ℤ; see project_tangent) and run the TaSK Lanczos recursion of H from it. The poles and weights of the spectral function are returned as a TaSKResult.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.task_spectrum"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.task_time_evolve-Tuple{TaSKResult, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"task_time_evolve(res::TaSKResult, t::Real; scale_by_b0 = false)\n\nTime-evolve the initial tangent vector within the stored Krylov basis: exp(-i H t) |phi0⟩.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.task_time_evolve"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.tdvp_correlator-Tuple{Any, MPSKit.QP, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Reference","text":"tdvp_correlator(H, qp::MPSKit.QP, times; alg = TDVP(), envs = nothing) -> Vector\n\nReal-time correlator C(t) = ⟨qp| exp(-i H t) |qp⟩ at the increasing times, obtained by evolving qp with the TDVP integrator within the quasiparticle tangent space. This is the time-domain reference for evaluate_correlator of a TaSK result (for a normalized qp, multiply by b0^2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.tdvp_correlator"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#MPSKitTaSK.tdvp_structure_factor-Tuple{Any, Any, MPSKit.AbstractMPS, AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Reference","text":"tdvp_structure_factor(H, O, gs, k_grid, ω_grid; σ = 0.05, dt = 0.1, tmax = 5 / σ, alg = TDVP(), envs = nothing, kwargs...)\n\nMomentum-resolved dynamical structure factor from TDVP time evolution of the projected states O_k|gs⟩ within the tangent space, Fourier transformed with a Gaussian window of width σ (see correlator_spectrum). This is directly comparable to the Gaussian broadening of the TaSK poles from dynamical_structure_factor. Remaining keyword arguments are passed to project_tangent. Returns a named tuple with k_grid, k_over_pi, omega_grid, times, S_kw (ω × k) and the correlators C_k(t).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitTaSK.tdvp_structure_factor"},{"category":"section","location":"index/#Index","page":"Index","text":"","title":"Index"},{"category":"section","location":"#MPSKitTaSK.jl","page":"Home","text":"MPSKitTaSK.jl implements the tangent-space Krylov (TaSK) method for dynamical spectral functions of finite matrix product states on top of MPSKit.jl (arXiv:2510.07279). A local (or momentum-resolved) operator applied to the ground state is projected onto the quasiparticle tangent space, and a Lanczos recursion of the effective excitation Hamiltonian yields the poles and weights of the spectral function. Abelian and non-abelian symmetries (e.g. SU2Irrep) of TensorKit.jl are supported, as are arbitrary N-site and charged operators.","title":"MPSKitTaSK.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"The package is not yet registered in the Julia general registry. It can be installed through the package manager with the following command:\n\npkg> add https://github.com/ManyBodyLab/MPSKitTaSK.jl","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Code-Samples","page":"Home","text":"using MPSKit, MPSKitModels, TensorKit\nusing MPSKitTaSK\n\n# ground state of the spin-1/2 Heisenberg chain with SU(2) symmetry\nL = 16\nH = heisenberg_XXX(SU2Irrep, FiniteChain(L); spin = 1 // 2)\nP = SU2Space(1 // 2 => 1)\nVs = [isodd(b) ? SU2Space(1 // 2 => 2, 3 // 2 => 1) : SU2Space(0 => 2, 1 => 2) for b in 1:(L - 1)]\ngs, envs = find_groundstate(FiniteMPS(fill(P, L), Vs), H, DMRG2(; trunc = truncrank(64), verbosity = 0))\n\n# spin structure factor ∑ₐ Sᵃᵃ(k, ω) at momentum k = π from one TaSK Lanczos run\nS = spin_vector_operator(SU2Irrep)\nres = task_spectrum(H, S, gs, π, TaSK(; krylovdim = 50); envs)\nres.energies, res.weights                      # poles and spectral weights (∑ weights = b0²)\n\nω = range(0, 3.5; length = 300)\nS_ω = broaden(res, ω; broadening = :gaussian, σ = 0.05)\n\n# full momentum-resolved S(k, ω) for k = 2πn/L\ndsf = dynamical_structure_factor(S, gs, H, 2π .* (0:(L - 1)) ./ L, ω; envs, broadening = :gaussian, sigma = 0.05)\n\nWith Plots.jl loaded, plot_spectral_function(dsf.results, dsf.k_over_pi; ω_grid = ω) shows the heatmap. A complete example, which also compares TaSK against TDVP time evolution in the tangent space, is examples/heisenberg_finite.jl:\n\njulia examples/heisenberg_finite.jl   # Julia ≥ 1.11 picks up the local package via [sources]","title":"Code Samples"},{"category":"section","location":"#License","page":"Home","text":"MPSKitTaSK.jl is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. By using or interacting with this software in any way, you agree to the license of this software.\n\n\n\nThis page was generated using Literate.jl.","title":"License"}]
